H y m e n o c h a e t e Lev. PEER CORFIXEN
D: Ruslsedersvamp. N: Broddsopp. S: Borstskinn. F: Vuotikat.
titre$Hymenochaete Nordic macromycetes 

com$adapt GF avril 2013

1,0$source : Nordic macromycetes 3 p 322

1,0$ Hymenochaete : Frb annual, resupinate to effused-reflexed, brown. Hymenophore smooth but brown setae can be seen with hand-lens, often stratified or multi-layered. Trama layer present or absent. Frb black in KOH. ///Hyphal system monomitic. Hyphae yellow to brown, often thick-walled. Clamps absent. Setae present in hymenium, in a few species also in the trama, subulate or acuminate. Sp ovoid to allantoid, hyaline (often difficult to find). ///On wood of deciduous and coniferous trees, causing a white rot , in a few species as pocket rot.///At least 5 species in the Nordic countries. Lit.: Jahn 1971

1,2 $ Frb effused-reflexed; trama distinct and compressed
1,3 $ Frb strictly effused; trama thin, > 75  µm or ± open
2,0 $ Frb easily separable from the substrate, orbiculate to widely effused, often with reflexed margin; hymenium greyish brown, mostly not stratified. Sp 4.5 - 7 x 1.5-3.5  µm , cylindric to allantoid; hymenial setae 50-100 * 8 - 18  µm, acuminate, pitted on apex; solitary tramal setae 90-285 " 7 - 1 3  µm (Fig. 712). - On bushes, especially Salix and Corylus, never on Quercus. HJ 128, R&H 197, B&K II 297. $ H. tabacina (Fr.) Lev.
2,0 $ Frb hardly separable from the substrate, attached by a central depression, often confluent and imbricate; hymenium reddish brown, mostly stratified. 323 Sp 4 - 6 . 5 * 2.5-3.5  µm , ellipsoid; hymenial setae 30-75 " 4 - 11  µm, subulate, smooth on apex; solitary tramal setae rare, 60-80 * 4  µm (Fig. 711). - On Quercus, mostly old stumps, causing a pocket rot. Phil 235, R & H 198, B&K II 296. $ H. rubiginosa (Fr.) Lev. (Stereum ferrugineum Fr.)
3,0 $ Trama distinct, of loosely interwoven hyphae, alternating with setal layers. Frb effused, pale yellow, cinnamon or chestnut. Sp 5.5-6.5 * 1.5-2.5  µm, allantoid t o reniform; hymenial setae 60-180 * 4-9  µm , s u b u l a t e , smooth on apex; tramal setae absent (Fig. 708). - Causing a pocket rot on deciduous trees. H J 130, B&K II 292. $ H. cinnamomea (Fr.) Bres. ( // . arida P. Karst.)
3,4 $ Trama almost absent; setae smaller 4
4,0 $ Frb effused, dark chocolate to bay, normally not cracked. Hymenial setae 40-100 " 6 - 8  µm , subulate, smooth on apex. Sp 4.5 - 6.5 * 2-3  µm , ellipsoid to cylindric (Fig. 710). - On rotten wood of coniferous trees, in northern areas also on Salix, in s southern areas also on Quercus. B&K II 294. D: r. N: 1 - 4 o-r. S: 2 - 3 r-o. F: 2 - 3 o-r. $ H. fuliginosa (Pers.) Bres. (H. subfuliginosa Bourdot & Galzin)
4,0 $ Frb effused, grey to milky coffee, normally cracked. Hymenial setae 40-100 x 6 - 14  µm, acuminate, pitted on apex. Sp 3.5-5 x 1-1.5  µm , cylindric (Fig. 709). - On various deciduous trees. B&K II 293. $ H. corrugata (Fr.) Lev.

